H1100.definition:
from H1097 (בְּלִי) and H3276 (יַעַל);(often in connection with H376 (אִישׁ), H802 (אִשָּׁה), H1121 (בֵּן), etc.)
without profit, worthlessness; by extension, destruction, wickedness
KJV: Belial, evil, naughty, ungodly (men), wicked.

H1102.definition:
a primitive root;
to muzzle
KJV: be held in.

H1103.definition:
a primitive root;
to pinch sycamore figs (a process necessary to ripen them)
KJV: gatherer.

H1104.definition:
a primitive root;
to make away with (specifically by swallowing); generally, to destroy
KJV: cover, destroy, devour, eat up, be at end, spend up, swallow down (up).

H1105.definition:
from H1104 (בָּלַע);
a gulp; figuratively, destruction
KJV: devouring, that which he hath swallowed up.

H1106.definition:
the same as H1105 (בֶּלַע);
Bela, the name of a place, also of an Edomite and of two Israelites
KJV: Bela.

H1108.definition:
patronymically from H1106 (בֶּלַע);
a Belaite (collectively) or descendants of Bela
KJV: Belaites.

H1109.definition:
probably from H1077 (בַּל) and H5971 (עַם); not (of the) people, i.e. foreigner;
Bilam, a Mesopotamian prophet; also a place in Palestine
KJV: Balaam, Bileam.

H1110.definition:
a primitive root;
to annihilate
KJV: (make) waste.

H1111.definition:
from H1110 (בָּלַק); waster;
Balak, a Moabitish king
KJV: Balak.

H1112.definition:
or בֵּלְאשַׁצַּרlemma בֵּלְאשַׁצּר missing vowel, corrected to בֵּלְאשַׁצַּר; of foreign origin (compare H1095 (בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּר));
Belshatstsar, a Babylonian king
KJV: Belshazzar.

H1113.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1112 (בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר)
{Belshatstsar, a Babylonian king}
KJV: Belshazzar.

H1114.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Bilshan, an Israelite
KJV: Bilshan.

H1115.definition:
constructive feminine of H1086 (בָּלָה) (equivalent to H1097 (בְּלִי));
properly, a failure of, i.e. (used only as a negative particle, usually with a prepositional prefix) not, except, without, unless, besides, because not, until, etc.
KJV: because un(satiable), beside, but, [phrase] continual, except, from, lest, neither, no more, none, not, nothing, save, that no, without.

H1116.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be high);
an elevation
KJV: height, high place, wave.

H1117.definition:
the same as H1116 (בָּמָה);
Bamah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bamah. See also H1120 (בָּמוֹת).

H1118.definition:
probably from H4107 (מָהַל) with prepositional prefix; with pruning;
Bimhal, an Israelite
KJV: Bimhal.

H1119.definition:
prolongation for prepositional prefix;
in, with, by, etc.
KJV: for, in into, through.

H1120.definition:
plural of H1116 (בָּמָה); heights; or (fully) בָּמוֹת בַּעַל; from the same and H1168 (בַּעַל); heights of Baal;
Bamoth or Bamoth-Baal, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Bamoth, Bamoth-baal.

H1121.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה);
a son (as a builder of the family name), in the widest sense (of literal and figurative relationship, including grandson, subject, nation, quality or condition, etc., (like father or brother), etc.)
KJV: [phrase] afflicted, age, (Ahoh-) (Ammon-) (Hachmon-) (Lev-) ite, (anoint-) ed one, appointed to, ([phrase]) arrow, (Assyr-) (Babylon-) (Egypt-) (Grec-) ian, one born, bough, branch, breed, [phrase] (young) bullock, [phrase] (young) calf, [idiom] came up in, child, colt, [idiom] common, [idiom] corn, daughter, [idiom] of first, [phrase] firstborn, foal, [phrase] very fruitful, [phrase] postage, [idiom] in, [phrase] kid, [phrase] lamb, ([phrase]) man, meet, [phrase] mighty, [phrase] nephew, old, ([phrase]) people, [phrase] rebel, [phrase] robber, [idiom] servant born, [idiom] soldier, son, [phrase] spark, [phrase] steward, [phrase] stranger, [idiom] surely, them of, [phrase] tumultuous one, [phrase] valiant(-est), whelp, worthy, young (one), youth.

H1122.definition:
the same as H1121 (בֵּן);
Ben, an Israelite
KJV: Ben.

H1123.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1121 (בֵּן)
{a son (as a builder of the family name), in the widest sense}
KJV: child, son, young.

H1124.definition:
(Aramaic) or בְּנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1129 (בָּנָה);
to build
KJV: build, make.

H1125.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H40 (אֲבִימֶלֶךְ); (the) son of Abinadab;
Ben-Abinadab, an Israelite
KJV: the son of Abinadab.

H1126.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H205 (אָוֶן); son of my sorrow;
Ben-Oni, the original name of Benjamin
KJV: Ben-oni.

H1127.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H1397 (גֶּבֶר); son of (the) hero;
Ben-Geber, an Israelite
KJV: the son of Geber.

H1128.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and a derivative of H1856 (דָּקַר); son of piercing (or of a lance);
Ben-Deker, an Israelite
KJV: the son of Dekar.

H1129.definition:
a primitive root;
to build (literally and figuratively)
KJV: (begin to) build(-er), obtain children, make, repair, set (up), [idiom] surely.

H1130.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H1908 (הֲדַד); son of Hadad;
Ben-Hadad, the name of several Syrian kings
KJV: Benhadad.

H1131.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה); built up;
Binnui, an Israelite
KJV: Binnui.

H1132.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H2105 (זוֹחֵת); son of Zocheth;
Ben-Zocheth, an Israelite
KJV: Ben-zoketh.

H1133.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H2354 (חוּר); son of Chur;
Ben-Chur, an Israelite
KJV: the son of Hur.

H1134.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H2428 (חַיִל); son of might;
Ben-Chail, an Israelite
KJV: Ben-hail.

H1135.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H2605 (חָנָן); son of Chanan;
Ben-Chanan, an Israelite
KJV: Ben-hanan.

H1136.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H2617 (חֵסֵד); son of kindness;
Ben-Chesed, an Israelite
KJV: the son of Hesed.

H1137.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה); built;
Bani, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Bani.

H1138.definition:
or (fuller) בּוּנִי; from H1129 (בָּנָה); built;
Bunni or Buni, an Israelite
KJV: Bunni.

H1139.definition:
from the plural construction of H1121 (בֵּן) and H1300 (בָּרָק);
sons of lightning, Bene-berak, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bene-barak.

H1140.definition:
feminine from H1129 (בָּנָה);
a structure
KJV: building.

H1141.definition:
or בּנָיָהוּ; (prolonged) from H1129 (בָּנָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has built;
Benajah, the name of twelve Israelites
KJV: Benaiah.

H1142.definition:
from the plural of H1121 (בֵּן) and H3292 (יַעֲקָן); sons of Yaakan;
Bene-Jaakan, a place in the Desert
KJV: Bene-jaakan.

H1143.definition:
dual of H996 (בֵּין);
a double interval, i.e. the space between two armies
KJV: [phrase] champion.

H1144.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H3225 (יָמִין); son of (the) right hand;
Binjamin, youngest son of Jacob; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory
KJV: Benjamin.

H1145.definition:
sometimes (with the article inserted) בֵּן־הַיּמִינִי; with H376 (אִישׁ) inserted (1 Samuel 9:1) בֶּן־אִישׁ ימִינִי; son of a man of Jemini; or shortened אִישׁ יְמִינִי; (1 Samuel 9:4; Esther 2:5) a man of Jemini, or (1 Samuel 20:1) simply יְמִינִיxlit Yᵉmînîy corrected to Yᵉmîynîy; a Jeminite; (plural) בְּנֵי יְמִינִיxlit Bᵉnîy corrected to Bᵉnêy; patron from H1144 (בִּנְיָמִין);
a Benjaminite, or descendent of Benjamin
KJV: Benjamite, of Benjamin.

H1146.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה);
an edifice
KJV: building.

H1147.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1146 (בִּנְיָן)
{an edifice}
KJV: building.

H1148.definition:
probably from H1121 (בֵּן) with pron. suff.; our son;
Beninu, an Israelite
KJV: Beninu.

H1149.definition:
(Aramaic) of uncertain affinity;
to be enraged
KJV: be angry.

H1150.definition:
or בִּנְעָה; of uncertain derivation;
Bina or Binah, an Israelite
KJV: Binea, Bineah.

H1151.definition:
from H1121 (בֵּן) and H5971 (עַם) with pronomial suffix; son of my people;
Ben-Ammi, a son of Lot
KJV: Ben-ammi.

H1152.definition:
from H5475 (סוֹד) and H3050 (יָהּ) with prepositional prefix; in (the) counsel of Jehovah;
Besodejah, an Israelite
KJV: Besodeiah.

H1153.definition:
from H947 (בּוּס); domineering;
Besai, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Besai.

H1154.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be sour;
an immature grape
KJV: unripe grape.

H1155.definition:
from the same as H1154 (בֶּסֶר)
{an immature grape}
KJV: sour grape.

H1156.definition:
(Aramaic) or בְּעָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1158 (בָּעָה);
to seek or ask
KJV: ask, desire, make (petition), pray, request, seek.

H1157.definition:
from H5704 (עַד) with prepositional prefix;
in up to or over against; generally at, beside, among, behind, for, etc.
KJV: about, at by (means of), for, over, through, up (-on), within.

H1158.definition:
a primitive root;
to gush over, i.e. to swell; (figuratively) to desire earnestly; by implication to ask
KJV: cause, inquire, seek up, swell out.

H1159.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1156 (בְּעָא);
a request
KJV: petition.

H1160.definition:
from H1197 (בָּעַר) (in the sense of burning); a lamp;
Beor, the name of the father of an Edomitish king; also of that of Balaam
KJV: Beor.

H1161.definition:
masculine plural from H1204 (בָּעַת);
alarms
KJV: terrors.

H1162.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Boaz, the ancestor of David; also the name of a pillar in front of the temple
KJV: Boaz.

H1163.definition:
a primitive root;
to trample down, i.e. (figuratively) despise
KJV: kick.

H1164.definition:
from H1158 (בָּעָה);
a prayer
KJV: grave.

H1165.definition:
from H1197 (בָּעַר) (in the sense of eating);
cattle
KJV: beast, cattle.

H1167.definition:
from H1166 (בָּעַל);
a master; hence, a husband, or (figuratively) owner (often used with another noun in modifications of this latter sense)
KJV: [phrase] archer, [phrase] babbler, [phrase] bird, captain, chief man, [phrase] confederate, [phrase] have to do, [phrase] dreamer, those to whom it is due, [phrase] furious, those that are given to it, great, [phrase] hairy, he that hath it, have, [phrase] horseman, husband, lord, man, [phrase] married, master, person, [phrase] sworn, they of.

H1168.definition:
the same as H1167 (בַּעַל);
Baal, a Phoenician deity
KJV: Baal, (plural) Baalim.

H1169.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1167 (בַּעַל)
{a master; hence, a husband,}
KJV: [phrase] chancellor.

H1170.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H1285 (בְּרִית); Baal of (the) covenant;
Baal-Berith, a special deity of the Shechemites
KJV: Baal-berith.

H1171.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H1409 (גָּד); Baal of Fortune;
Baal-Gad, a place in Syria
KJV: Baal-gad.

H1172.definition:
feminine of H1167 (בַּעַל);
a mistress
KJV: that hath, mistress.

H1173.definition:
the same as H1172 (בַּעֲלָה);
Baalah, the name of three places in Palestine
KJV: Baalah.

H1174.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and H1995 (הָמוֹן); possessor of a multitude;
Baal-Hamon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-hamon.

H1175.definition:
plural of H1172 (בַּעֲלָה); mistresses;
Bealoth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bealoth, in Aloth (by mistake for a plural from H5927 (עָלָה) with prepositional prefix).

H1176.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H2070 (זְבוּב); Baal of (the) Fly;
Baal-Zebub, a special deity of the Ekronites
KJV: Baal-zebub.

H1177.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and H2603 (חָנַן); possessor of grace;
Baal-Chanan, the name of an Edomite, also of an Israelite
KJV: Baal-hanan.

H1178.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and a modification of H2691 (חָצֵר); possessor of a village;
Baal-Chatsor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-hazor.

H1179.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and H2768 (חֶרְמוֹן); possessor of Hermon;
Baal-Chermon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-hermon.

H1180.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) with pron. suff.; my master;
Baali, a symbolical name for Jehovah
KJV: Baali.

H1181.definition:
from the plural of H1168 (בַּעַל) and the plural of H1116 (בָּמָה); Baals of (the) heights;
Baale-Bamoth, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: lords of the high places.

H1182.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H3045 (יָדַע); Baal has known;
Beeljada, an Israelite
KJV: Beeliada.

H1183.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah (is) master;
Bealjah, an Israelite
KJV: Bealiah.

H1184.definition:
from the plural of H1167 (בַּעַל) and H3063 (יְהוּדָה); masters of Judah;
Baale-Jehudah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baale of Judah.

H1185.definition:
probably from a derivative of H5965 (עָלַס) with prepositional prefix; in exultation;
Baalis, an Ammonitish king
KJV: Baalis.

H1186.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H4583 (מָעוֹן); Baal of (the) habitation (of) (compare H1010 (בֵּית בַּעַל מְעוֹן));
Baal-Meon, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Baal-meon.

H1187.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H6465 (פְּעוֹר); Baal of Peor;
Baal-Peor, a Moabitish deity
KJV: Baal-peor.

H1188.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and the plural of H6556 (פֶּרֶץ); possessor of breaches;
Baal-Peratsim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-perazim.

H1189.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H6828 (צָפוֹן) (in the sense of cold) (according to others an Egyptian form of Typhon, the destroyer); Baal of winter;
Baal-Tsephon, a place in Eqypt
KJV: Baal-zephon.

H1190.definition:
from H1168 (בַּעַל) and H8031 (שָׁלִשָׁה);
Baal of Shalishah, Baal-Shalishah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-shalisha.

H1191.definition:
a modification of H1172 (בַּעֲלָה); mistressship;
Baalath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baalath.

H1192.definition:
from H1172 (בַּעֲלָה) and H875 (בְּאֵר); mistress of a well;
Baalath-Beer, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baalath-beer.

H1193.definition:
from H1167 (בַּעַל) and H8558 (תָּמָר); possessor of (the) palm-tree;
Baal-Tamar, a place in Palestine
KJV: Baal-tamar.

H1194.definition:
probably a contraction of H1010 (בֵּית בַּעַל מְעוֹן);
Beon, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Beon.

H1195.definition:
the same as H1196 (בַּעֲנָה);
Banana, the name of four Israelite
KJV: Baana, Baanah.

H1198.definition:
from H1197 (בָּעַר);
properly, foot (as consumed); i.e. (by exten.) of cattle brutishness; (concretely) stupid
KJV: brutish (person), foolish.

H1199.definition:
from H1198 (בַּעַר); brutish;
Baara, an Israelitish woman
KJV: Baara.
